{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfrwudak","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 2 Offline","year":2009,"examDate":2009,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"stability-of-intermediate","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pthe-correct-stability-order-of-the-following-resonance-st-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-hvbqgmoiclsvd5ul","content":"<p>The correct stability order of the following resonance structures is</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lft4wpxu/5a1be786-6809-4535-91e7-c6635606981e/c9ebf320-cde2-11ed-9ce1-7bd2ccf24231/file-1lft4wpxv.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lft4wpxu/5a1be786-6809-4535-91e7-c6635606981e/c9ebf320-cde2-11ed-9ce1-7bd2ccf24231/file-1lft4wpxv.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 9 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lft4wpxu/5a1be786-6809-4535-91e7-c6635606981e/c9ebf320-cde2-11ed-9ce1-7bd2ccf24231/file-1lft4wpxv.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lft4wpxu/5a1be786-6809-4535-91e7-c6635606981e/c9ebf320-cde2-11ed-9ce1-7bd2ccf24231/file-1lft4wpxv.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lft4wpxu/5a1be786-6809-4535-91e7-c6635606981e/c9ebf320-cde2-11ed-9ce1-7bd2ccf24231/file-1lft4wpxv.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lft4wpxu/5a1be786-6809-4535-91e7-c6635606981e/c9ebf320-cde2-11ed-9ce1-7bd2ccf24231/file-1lft4wpxv.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lft4wpxu/5a1be786-6809-4535-91e7-c6635606981e/c9ebf320-cde2-11ed-9ce1-7bd2ccf24231/file-1lft4wpxv.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lft4wpxu/5a1be786-6809-4535-91e7-c6635606981e/c9ebf320-cde2-11ed-9ce1-7bd2ccf24231/file-1lft4wpxv.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"(I) > (II) > (IV) > (III)"},{"identifier":"B","content":"(I) > (III) > (II) > (IV)"},{"identifier":"C","content":"(II) > (I) > (III) > (IV)"},{"identifier":"D","content":"(III) > (I) > (IV) > (II)"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>Among the resonance structures, the more stable ones are those with:</p>\n<p>(i) more number of covalent bonds</p>\n<p>(ii) all the atoms having octet of electrons complete,</p>\n<p>(iii) less separation of opposite charges and more dispersal of charge.</p>\n<p>Based on these, the order of stability of the resonance structures is (I) > (III) > (II) > (IV).</p>"}]}